{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-257-wall","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/sec-257-wall","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=sec-257-wall","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=sec-257-wall","span":{"end_byte":94432,"end_line":941,"start_byte":69149,"start_line":743},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.prop-canon&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.prop-canon&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.prop-canon&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.prop-canon&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.prop-canon","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-canon"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-canon"],"id":"long.prop-canon","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 2.2 (Uniqueness under the stated finite conditions)","locator":"Long record Proposition 2.2, p. 27, label prop:canon","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Put $G=\\mathrm{greedyMersenneSupport}(1/2)$, $w_n=(2^n-1)^{-1}$ and $R_d=\\sum_{n>d}w_n$. The following are three separate uniqueness statements.*\n\n1.  *If $D\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$ and $X_D(2)\\le1/2\\le X_D(2)+R_d$, then $D=G\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$.*\n\n2.  *If $c\\ge4$, $D\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,c-1\\}$ and $0<1/2-X_D(2)<w_c$, then $D=G\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,c-1\\}$.*\n\n3.  *Let positive integer weights $v_1,\\ldots,v_k$ satisfy $v_i\\ge g+\\sum_{j>i}v_j$ for a positive integer $g$. For a nonnegative integer target $T$, let $y^*$ be the word obtained by visiting these weights in order and taking each when it fits. An admissible Boolean word $y$ has $0\\le T-\\sum_i y_iv_i<g$ if and only if $y=y^*$ and $0\\le T-\\sum_i y_i^*v_i<g$.*\n\n*Part (iii) gives uniqueness under the small-remainder condition, not existence. Theorem 6.100 gives a one-weight counterexample to dropping that condition.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.prop-canon","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.prop-canon","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.prop-canon%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.remainder_lt_gap_iff_eq_integerGreedyBits%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.prop-canon%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.BooleanMobiusGreedyReduction.remainder_lt_gap_iff_eq_integerGreedyBits%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b0